{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee","id":945466,"title":"A Clutch of Dragons: Dragon-Blooded Melee","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T08:14:51-07:00","id":945466,"title":"A Clutch of Dragons: Dragon-Blooded Melee","content":"I have been writing some Dragon-Blooded Charms. Quite a few of them, actually.<br /> <br /> Since I started <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\">A Clutch of Dragons</a>, the Ability I have been asked most about has been Melee, so I thought it deserved its own thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X5ZeD-jSQGl3GzIg-ispWjo6ZHOrccC0noucnNHG14w/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Melee </a>is Ability number 14, and has 39 Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Fire</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Burning Soul Sword</span></b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1a; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The Exalt infuses her weapon with the power of her anima, sharpening it on her resolve and surrounding it with an expression of her elemental wrath. This Charm enhances one of the Exalt\u2019s Melee weapons. Its burning attacks double (Essence) 9s on a withering damage roll and a single 10 on a decisive damage roll.<br /> <br /> Burning Soul Sword can be used to enhance non-ranged Martial Arts form weapons of a style the Dragon-Blood knows that lack the Melee tag, such as hook swords or war fans, provided she has a Martial Arts rating of 3+ in the style.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Dragon-Graced Weapon</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins:Melee 1, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The Exalt summons a burst of flames that adds (Melee) to the raw damage of a withering attack, or one die to the damage of a decisive attack. At Initiative 11+, she adds two dice to her decisive damage instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Blinding Spark Distraction</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 2i; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dragon-Graced Weapon<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s weapon strikes a shower of sparks as it parries her opponent\u2019s attack, intensifying in an instant to a dazzling flare. After a successful parry, the attacker suffers a penalty to all sight-based actions equal to the number of successes by which his attack failed to meet the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Defence, to a maximum of her (Melee/2) rounded up. This penalty lasts until the end of the attacker\u2019s next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Raging Firestorm Blade</b></span><br /> Cost: 6m, 3a; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dragon-Graced Weapon<br /> <br /> The intense flames of the Exalt\u2019s anima condense over the edge of her weapon and release at the moment of contact, cleaving through her opponent in a devastating concentrated explosion.. While the Dragon-Blood\u2019s anima is at bonfire, she may discharge it to convert all post-soak damage dice of a withering attack to successes, or (Essence) dice on a decisive damage roll to successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Stoking Bonfire Style</b></span><br /> Cost: 1a; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Uniform<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> When attacking an opponent of lower initiative, the Exalt may expend an anima level to reduce the cost of the Melee excellency to 1m per two dice added or rerolled. Once per scene unless reset by landing a decisive attack and building back up to 10+ initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Song of Steel and Embers</span></b><br /> Cost: 1m, 1i; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood learns to add the ferocity of fire to her weapon\u2019s blows, driving her foes back under her relentless assault. Her attack inflicts two points of onslaught penalty rather than one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Way of the Dragon</span></b><br /> Cost: 1i; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Withering-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> <br /> The Fire Dragon\u2019s blade is relentless and unhesitating, blurring from one attack into the next. After a successful withering attack, she can spend one Initiative to add one bonus die to a pool she can expend on future Melee attacks. The Dragon-Blood may retain a maximum of (Melee) dice in this pool, and they are lost at the end of the scene, when she resets to base initiative or when she is crashed. If her withering attack crashes her opponent, her anima also flares up by one level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Fuel for the Pyre</span></b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Way of the Dragon<br /> <br /> The attacks of the Exalt\u2019s enemies only fuel the blaze of her assault. When she successfully parries an attack, she may use this Charm to negate any onslaught penalty it caused and add one to the dice pool of Way of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Molten Iron Defence</span></b><br /> Cost: -; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Permanent<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Fuel for the Pyre<br /> <br /> As the Dragon-Blood\u2019s anima builds, her weapon glows cherry-red with the intensity of her resolve, and strife only further kindles her flames. Whenever the Dragon-Blood parries an attack while her anima is at glowing level or above, she gains a mote for each 10 on her attacker\u2019s dice pool, to a maximum of half the motes she spent on raising her Defence using the Melee Excellency. If her anima is at bonfire level, she also counts 9s.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Brazen Blade Feint</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m, 3i, 1a; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> <br /> Sensing a weakness in her opponent\u2019s defence, the Exalt\u2019s unleashes a flashy, dazzling series of attacks, distracting her foe and opening an opportunity for an ally to strike a subtler and more deadly blow. Brazen Blade Feint generates a special distract gambit that grants an ally Initiative equal to successes on the activation roll. The cost of the gambit is replaced by the cost of this Charm. Once per scene, unless reset by landing a decisive attack that benefits from a distract gambit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Crimson Lotus Rebuke</b></span><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Clash, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Blinding Spark Distraction, Molten Iron Defence<br /> <br /> With swiftness and fury, the Dragon-Blood meets her opponent\u2019s attack head on. She can reflexively clash a decisive attack, regardless of her position in the turn order. If she is successful, she can use Molten Iron Defence to regain up to half of the motes she spent on her Excellency, regaining one mote for each 9s and 10s on her opponent\u2019s attack. The clash attack granted by this Charm counts as her action for the round, and she cannot make another. If she has already acted this round, then it counts as her action for her next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Fire-Breathing Dragon Spirit</span></b><br /> Cost: 1a; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Withering-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Crimson Lotus Rebuke<br /> <br /> Focusing her wrath, the Exalt channels her fiery aura to augment her attack at the point of contact, ensuring that even her most extended strikes are delivered with lethal force. When the Dragon-Blood\u2019s attack rolls a number of successes exactly equal to her opponent\u2019s defence or his attack result in a clash, she may expend an anima level to activate the rerolls of the Melee Excellency without spending willpower and gain double 8s on rerolled dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode</span></b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1a; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Molten Iron Defence<br /> <br /> With explosive force and speed, the Dragon-Blood interposes her blade in the path of an incoming attack, deflecting even the surest strike at the last moment. This Charm is used after she is struck by a decisive attack, but before damage is rolled. The Dragon-Blood rolls her initiative in dice, doubling 10s, or doubling 9s against an opponent with lower initiative. Each success subtracts a die from the attack\u2019s raw damage. If the damage is reduced to zero, the attack counts as having being successfully parried for the purposes of the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Charms. In any case, both combatants reset to base initiative. The Dragon-Blood can add bonus dice gained from Way of the Dragon to her initiative roll, and if she negates all damage she can use Scintillating Chain Momentum to regain initiative after she resets to base as though she landed a decisive attack if she knows that Charm.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Exalt may use Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode when an ally being protected by her defend other action is struck with a decisive attack. The defence resolves in the same way, except it rolls and resets her defended ally\u2019s initiative instead of the Exalt\u2019s own. The ally must be a willing participant in this defence. The Dragon-Blood may not use Scintillating Chain Momentum to grant her ally initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Refining the Inner Blade</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1a; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Burning Soul Sword<br /> <br /> With a moment\u2019s concentration, the Dragon-Blood shapes a gleaming weapon from the raw stuff of her anima. This soul weapon takes the form of any mundane weapon with the Melee tag the Exalt desires, and is enhanced with the properties of Burning Soul Sword. It crumbles into ash and vanishes at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> As with Burning Soul Sword, Refining the Inner Blade can create Martial Arts form weapons with an Ability rating of 3+ in the style.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vanished in the Flames</span></b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Refining the Inner Blade<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood casts a weapon into the substance of her anima. The weapon appears to be consumed by her flames, leaving behind only dissipating ash and embers. At any time the Dragon-Blood may use Refining the Inner Blade to reform the weapon anew, wreathed in the fire of her anima. Its enhancement fades at the end of the scene, but the weapon remains as whole as it was before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Conflagration of Warding</span></b><br /> Cost:-; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> Type:Permanent<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode<br /> <br /> This Charm permanently enhances its prerequisite. When the Dragon-Blood uses Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode, allies within close range can each contribute up to their Melee in Initiative towards his defence. Dragon-Blooded allies can add (Melee+Essence) initiative. The Dragon-Blood herself may contribute Initiative towards her ward if she is using Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode as part of a defend other action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Scintillating Chain Momentum</b></span><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:None<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Fuel for the Pyre<br /> <br /> The Exalt\u2019s blade moves from attack to attack in a blur, only building in resolve and certainty as the onslaught progresses. After a successful decisive attack using bonus dice from Way of the Dragon, the Exalt may use Scintillating Chain Momentum to roll an equal number of dice and add the successes to her base initiative when she resets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Ringing Anvil Onslaught</b></span><br /> Cost: 6m (+1wp); Mins:Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Raging Firestorm Blade, Way of the Dragon<br /> <br /> Focusing on a single enemy, the Exalt\u2019s weapon moves in a blur, raising a fountain of sparks with a wild torrent of attacks, ringing together in one long, continuous note. After a successful withering attack, she may make another attack against the same enemy with a pool of (Melee + threshold success), up to a maximum of (Essence x 2) threshold successes, which cannot have dice added to it by any other magic except for Way of the Dragon. The Dragon-Blood may continue attacking until she misses or crashes her enemy. If she crashes her target she may pay a point of Willpower to follow through with a decisive attack at her full dice pool. Once per scene unless reset by achieving Initiative Shift.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Garda Wing Technique</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 3<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Ringing Anvil Onslaught<br /> <br /> Sword glowing in an incandescent arc, the Exalt cleaves through two enemies at once. She makes two decisive attacks against two separate opponents within close range, dealing damage of half her initiative rounded up to each.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Tempered In Blood</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 4<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Ringing Anvil Onslaught<br /> <br /> After a successful decisive attack against a crashed enemy, the Fire Dragon\u2019s anima flares to bonfire level and she immediately rolls (Charisma + Melee), adding the result to her initiative after she resets to base. This counts as Initiative Shift for the purposes of resetting its prerequisite. Once per scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragonfire Maelstrom Barrier</b></span><br /> Cost: (+3m); Mins:Melee 5, Essence 4<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode, Crimson Lotus Rebuke<br /> <br /> If her anima is at burning level or above, the Dragon-Blood can spend an additional 3m activating Crimson Lotus Rebuke to allow it to clash any incoming source of damage, including unblockable attacks, damaging spells and battlegroup ranged attacks. Her elemental aura sweeps out with her weapon\u2019s swing, scattering the attack harmlessly away in a torrent of dragonfire. If she successfully clashes an area attack, any allies who stand behind her are unaffected. Clashing a ranged attack doesn\u2019t let the Dragon-Blood strike back, but she gains a number of motes equal to her threshold successes, to a maximum of (Melee), and her anima flares up by one level. Sources of uncountable damage can be clashed as ranged attacks, using a base dice pool of 15. Ongoing sources of uncountable damage are quelled for the action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Final Flash Attack</b></span><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp, 3a; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 4<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Crimson Lotus Rebuke, Ringing Anvil Onslaught<br /> <br /> A halo of crackling heat and light plays over the Terrestrial\u2019s weapon for an instant before she swings, unleashing an incandescent wave of fiery Essence through the ranks of her foes, leaving only black ash in its wake. Using this Charm requires an initiative level of 15+. The Exalt rolls (Dexterity + Melee) as a decisive attack applied in a line against enemies out to long range, rerolling the full amount of dice allowed by the Melee excellency without spending additional Willpower or motes.. This line is wide enough to strike all opponents within one range band of one another. Obstacles in the way of the attack are blasted asunder, suffering the results of a feat of strength equal to the Exalt\u2019s attack successes, ignoring strength minimums, and the destruction can reduce or negate cover bonuses at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Everyone struck by the Final Flash Attack suffers (Essence +3) damage dice, doubling 10s on the damage roll, and is knocked prone and pushed back one range band away from the Dragon-Blood. Battle groups and titanic enemies that occupy multiple range bands instead suffer damage from her full initiative with double 9s. The Dragon-Blood resets to base initiative after the attack. Once per scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury</b></span><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp, 3a; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 4<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Fire-Breathing Dragon Spirit, Burning Soul Sword<br /> <br /> The Fire Dragon summons a mighty expression of her wrath; her anima explodes into a torrent of brilliant flames before sweeping around her blade and vanishing, visible only on the very edge of her weapon, rippling with heat and shining white with the all-annihilating intensity of a falling star. While this Charm is active, she adds her current anima level to her raw withering damage and doubles all 9s on the damage roll. Using Way of the Dragon after a successful withering attack no longer costs initiative. A decisive attack adds raw damage equal to the number of dice from Way of the Dragon that enhanced the attack pool and benefits from double 10s. The Charm ends as she resets to base after a successful decisive attack..<br /> <br /> If this Charm is used on a weapon enhanced by Burning Soul Sword or created using Refining the Inner Blade, its cost is reduced to 4m, 1wp, 2a.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>World-Bearing Cataclysm Edge</b></span><br /> Cost:-; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 5<br /> Type:Permanent<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration:Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dragonfire Maelstrom Barrier, Final Flash Attack<br /> <br /> If the Dragon-Blood successfully uses Dragonfire Maelstrom Barrier to clash a source of uncountable damage or a sufficiently spectacular and momentous ranged attack, such as a Death Ray spell or Nova Arrow Attack, she may immediately counterattack with Final Flash Attack, ignoring the once per scene restriction. As a general guideline, any area damaging Simple type attack Charm or Evocation with an Essence requirement of 3+ or attack spells of the Celestial and Solar circle should be sufficient to trigger this response.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Water</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Water-Shedding Sword</b></span><br /> Cost: 1i; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration:One turn<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The fighting style of the Water Dragons is graceful and balanced, able to keep elegant poise even under the direst circumstances. After hitting with a withering or decisive attack, the Dragon-Blood can shed a point of initiative in order to ignore a point of penalty to her Melee defence for the turn. This reduction is proactive: if she is not currently suffering from a penalty, she ignores the first point of penalty when it appears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Trickling Steel Technique</b></span><br /> Cost: 2m, 1i; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Withering-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Water-Shedding Sword<br /> <br /> With sinuous grace, the Water Dragon slips her weapon through the weakest point of her opponent\u2019s armour. She ignores a number of points of armour soak equal to her attack\u2019s threshold successes. If the attack is already Piercing, she may ignore the initiative cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Serpent-Blade Strike</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 1i; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Trickling Steel Technique<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s weapon seems to take on a life of its own, snaking through the air and bending impossibly around defences. The attack ignores the Defence bonus of the opponent\u2019s weapon and the full defence action. If the weapon is Flexible, this Charm costs only 2m, 1i.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Mirror of Cascading Rain</b></span><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Perilous<br /> Duration:Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Water-Shedding Sword<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s blade keeps perfect time with her opponent\u2019s as they dart back and forth in the deadly dance of swordplay, like raindrops falling against a still pool of water. The Terrestrial may ignore a number of points of penalty to her defence equal to the onslaught penalty her attacker shed on his turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Raindrop-Cutting Counter</b></span><br /> Cost: (+3m); Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Mirror of Cascading Rain<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood may end Mirror of Cascading Rain after successfully parrying any attack to reset her current onslaught penalty to zero. If she does so after parrying an attack while suffering an onslaught penalty of -3 or greater, she may spend 3m to make an immediate decisive counterattack with the number of successes by which her attacker failed to meet her Defense in bonus dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Twin Rivers Elision Flash</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp, 1a; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Raindrop-Cutting Counter<br /> <br /> The world slows to the beating of a heart, and the swordswoman\u2019s blade moves in a flash, striking low\u2026 and high. The Dragon-Blood\u2019s attack appears to impossibly occupy two spaces simultaneously. One of the attacks is a harmless illusion woven from the substance of the Exalt\u2019s anima, but which? The Exalt launches two decisive attacks, which are both rolled before proceeding to damage. If both are successful, she must choose one to discard. The attack inflicts a single point of onslaught, which is only counted after the attacks are resolved.<br /> <br /> At Melee 5+, Essence 4+, the Dragon-Blood may spend an additional 3m to generate two illusory attacks, for a total of three attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><b>Style-Countering Meditation</b></span><br /> Cost: 0m+, 1i+; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Perilous<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Raindrop-Cutting Counter<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood can adapt perfectly to an opponent\u2019s combat style. After parrying an attack bolstered by a Supplemental type Charm during the scene, the Exalt has sufficiently analysed her opponent\u2019s technique to be able to counteract it with her own. Against future attacks using the Charm, she may pay a point of initiative and a number of motes equal to the mote cost of the Charm to negate its effects. Due to the complexities and mental demands involved in reading and analyzing a target so thoroughly, it suffers from diminishing returns. Each time she uses this Charm during a scene, its initiative cost increases by one. Style-Countering Meditation cannot be used against the Excellency Charm of any Ability, nor can it be used against spells or Evocations.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Earth</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Diamond-Cutting Sword</b></span><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> Earthly Essence courses over the Exalt\u2019s weapon, hardening it briefly to an edge that can defy any bulwark. After a successful hit, she rolls (Melee) dice and ignores a number of points of her opponent\u2019s Hardness equal to her successes.<br /> <br /> If the Dragon-Blood is faced with an effect that would destroy her mundane weapon (such as Octavian\u2019s Invincible Iron Bastion), she may use this Charm Reflexively to briefly endow her weapon with the durability of an artifact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Jade Phalanx Style</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins:Melee 1, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Uniform<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The Earth Dragon is a bastion unto herself, retaining an invincible defence even in the fiercest combat. She may flurry an attack with a full defence or defend other action and suffers no penalty to defence for doing so. If she has a weapon with the Shield tag, this Charm costs 2m.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Threshing Floor Technique</b></span><br /> Cost:4m; Mins:Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Withering-Only<br /> Duration:One tick<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Jade Phalanx Style<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood coordinates her allies in a series of destabilizing blows against her enemy, wearing down his defences. Her attack ignores a number of points of her target\u2019s soak equal to his current onslaught penalty, as do any attacks her target suffers for the remainder of the tick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>All For One</b></span><br /> Cost:4m, 1wp; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:One tick<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Threshing Floor Technique<br /> <br /> Acting in unison, the Dragon-Blood and her allies strike a deadly combined blow against their foe. She declares use of this Charm at the beginning of a tick on which she and at least one ally are in a position to attack a specific enemy with a decisive attack. The Dragon-Blood acts last during the tick. Any ally who attacks the enemy during the tick can announce that they are contributing to the effect of All For One. If he hits the target, his Initiative is recorded and he resets to base Initiative without proceeding to damage. When the Dragon-Blood herself attacks the target at the end of the tick, she gains all the recorded initiative from previously successful attacks, doubles 10s on the decisive damage roll, doubles one 9 for each failed attempt to contribute to the attack, and doubles an 8 for each successful one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Thousand-Ton Hammer Smash</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Jade Phalanx Style<br /> <br /> Filling her weapon with pulverizing weight, the Dragon-Blood delivers a mighty blow. She doubles 10s on decisive damage, or double 9s on all damage against a prone enemy. The attack becomes Smashing. If the weapon already has the Smashing tag, the attack incurs no Defence or Initiative penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>All Things in Time</b></span><br /> Cost: 1wp; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Thousand-Ton Hammer Smash<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood delays her action to act last during the round. For every hostile character with lower initiative than her, she gains 2 raw damage to her decisive attack when it finally arrives, to a maximum of 10 damage. Characters who delay their attacks to act at the same time as the Dragon-Blood or who also use this Charm or a similar one act simultaneously on the final tick of the action. Once per scene unless reset by using a full defence action for three consecutive turns without being crashed.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Air</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Five Winds Edge</span></b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1a, 2i; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual, Branching:Brawl<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The wind answers the call of the Child of Mela, condensing into a pellucid replica of her fist or weapon to flash through the air and strike her foe. Five Winds Edge enhances a Brawl or Melee withering or decisive attack, allowing it to be made at short range with the weapon profile of a Thrown weapon. A successful Grapple gambit made with this Charm can only Throw/Slam or Release before the magic dissipates.<br /> <br /> At Melee 4+, Essence 3+, the Dragon-Blood may pay an additional 2m, 1a to attack out to medium range.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Steel Thunderbolt Draw</b></span><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins:Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Uniform<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:None<br /> <br /> The swordswoman can flurry a ready weapon action with a melee attack with no Defence or dice pool penalty. If she wins Join Battle and does so on her first action, she gains bonus dice on her attack equal to the amount by which her Initiative exceeds that of her fastest adversary.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-07-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T11:46:20-07:00","id":945579,"title":"","content":"OH man this is really cool sounding. And seeing them able to block uncountable and unblockable is nice. I never liked that they couldn't in 2e without absurd requirements beyond high essence<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:13:16-07:00","id":945616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945579#post945579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH man this is really cool sounding. And seeing them able to block uncountable and unblockable is nice. I never liked that they couldn't in 2e without absurd requirements beyond high essence</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unblockable is less of a balance point in Ex3 because Charms are far more diverse in the ways they function. Terrestrials as I have designed them have some access to Charms that can defend against Uncountable damage, but they are typically E4+, more expensive and less reliable than their Solar counterparts. There are some exceptions, but there's nothing like Heavenly Guardian Defence that lets you swat a meteor out of the sky every turn without effort. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:41:35-07:00","id":945639,"title":"","content":"If the Dragon-Blooded using All For One misses his attack, are all of the previously successful attacks wasted? if so, that sounds a bit too risky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:57:47-07:00","id":945649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945639#post945639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Dragon-Blooded using All For One misses his attack, are all of the previously successful attacks wasted? if so, that sounds a bit too risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a high risk/reward combination attack. It's not useful in every circumstance, but it's death to big tough monsters with middling to poor defences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:07:46-07:00","id":945654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945616#post945616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, unblockable is less of a balance point in Ex3 because Charms are far more diverse in the ways they function. Terrestrials as I have designed them have some access to Charms that can defend against Uncountable damage, but they are typically E4+, more expensive and less reliable than their Solar counterparts. There are some exceptions, but there's nothing like Heavenly Guardian Defence that lets you swat a meteor out of the sky every turn without effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i like that a lot more. I always disliked the whole &quot;well they aren't THAT exalted so ... whatever they can't have the cool toys either&quot;. I feel no matter what situation it is, the presence of an exalt on your side should be legitimate hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T16:51:01-07:00","id":945745,"title":"","content":"As always, I really like this work. It's just so consistently excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:24:51-07:00","id":945787,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good, I like it. I'll examine it more in depth and see if I have any specific criticisms, but good job","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:10:27-07:00","id":945817,"title":"","content":"Where's Wood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:36:11-07:00","id":945999,"title":"","content":"Ah, hell, I've just been checking the hub thread and missed this one entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945817#post945817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's Wood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Ability has had some aspects left out of it where they don't resonate as strongly, so this is just following the pattern.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I posted this to the hub thread, but for discussion's sake I guess I'll add it here:<br /> <br /> So, seeing that Melee is up now, I gave it a look, and I think the vast majority of it is awesome work. I particularly like the clash charm + final flash and how that incentivizes Terrestrials to dunk on Wyld abominations and the like. On the other hand, I thought Portentious Comet-Deflecting Mode was <i>super</i> weak when I first read it (and I kind of still think it is), but on re-reading Countless Coils Evasion's Terrestrial mode (which seems to be roughly what it was balanced against?), it's actually significantly cheaper, has slightly better damage mitigation potential (from the potential double 9's), doesn't have the 'incompatible with other effects that lower decisive damage' rider (oversight, or intended?), and it has lower pre-reqs. <br /> <br /> I mean, now that I write all that out it seems like a good deal, but something still feels off somehow...<br /> <br /> I guess it just feelsbadman that you'll rarely ever get the full parry from it? I mean, even in a generous but not a-typical situation where you have 15 initiative, and a full 5 stacks built up for Way of the Dragon vs a 12 dice decisive, it's just about a coin flip whether you completely negate it or not. Maybe some sort of trigger (locked by Essence requirements) to save your Way of the Dragon stacks from getting lost when you reset to base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T02:29:53-07:00","id":946032,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945817#post945817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's Wood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like serGregness said, no Ability has Charms of all five Elements (except Craft, which ended up something of an anomaly). You'll notice that Air Melee is barely there at two Charms, and Earth and Water are far smaller than Fire. I never intended the distribution to be equal for every Ability, but hopefully it should be equal overall. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=945999#post945999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I thought Portentious Comet-Deflecting Mode was <i>super</i> weak when I first read it (and I kind of still think it is), but on re-reading Countless Coils Evasion's Terrestrial mode (which seems to be roughly what it was balanced against?), it's actually significantly cheaper, has slightly better damage mitigation potential (from the potential double 9's), doesn't have the 'incompatible with other effects that lower decisive damage' rider (oversight, or intended?), and it has lower pre-reqs.<br /> <br /> I mean, now that I write all that out it seems like a good deal, but something still feels off somehow...<br /> <br /> I guess it just feelsbadman that you'll rarely ever get the full parry from it? I mean, even in a generous but not a-typical situation where you have 15 initiative, and a full 5 stacks built up for Way of the Dragon vs a 12 dice decisive, it's just about a coin flip whether you completely negate it or not. Maybe some sort of trigger (locked by Essence requirements) to save your Way of the Dragon stacks from getting lost when you reset to base?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've hit on the issue directly. I'm trying to write as much in balance with DBs as presented in the QCs and MA Charms as possible, but Countless Coils Evasion is a real shitshow. At a stroke the Terrestrial keyword makes it flatly half as effective and makes it once per scene. I was compelled to edge in a few side benefits to Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode to make it more palatable. In most circumstances it will only mitigate but not perfectly stop a decisive attack, though this can easily mean the difference between life and death. <br /> <br /> The upgrade of Conflagration of Warding makes the defence more workable when your friends can work together to ward off a doomcombo decisive attack. It costs everyone initiative, but ups your odds considerably. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:54:00-07:00","id":948249,"title":"","content":"Well, with my most serious question addressed, I do have a few other more mechanically fiddly questions to clear up some of these charm interactions:<br /> <br /> Way of the Dragon: These are Charm dice, right? So in a vacuum (ignoring the other melee charms that interact with it, such as PCDM), the main practical benefit is that this saves you motes on the attack? Also, the 'After a successful withering attack' bit means that this is one of those charms that you don't have to declare before rolls happen?<br /> <br /> Crimson Lotus Rebuke: Since using this charm takes up your next combat action if you've already gone this round, what happens if, say, three different people try to stick you with a Decisive attack in the same round and you try to clash them all? Do you lose only your next action, or the next three?<br /> <br /> Garda Wing Technique: The attacks are rolled seperately, right? Not one roll applied to both targets? Do both attacks have to be augmented by charms separately?<br /> <br /> Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury: The double 9's benefit to decisive attacks is on the to-hit portion, not damage? The wording is a little unclear so I'm not entirely sure.<br /> <br /> World-Bearing Cataclysm Edge: The Final Flash counterattack is still paid for as normal, not free, right?<br /> <br /> Twin-Rivers Elision Flash: Not actually a mechanics question, but back in your dodge charmset, most of the various afterimage anima trickery was air-aspected, so I'm curious why you made something which seems very similar into a water charm here.<br /> <br /> I'm really enjoying the hell out of your work overall, and I expect to put it to some use in my campaign in the coming weeks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","user":"serGregness","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:45:32-07:00","id":948484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way of the Dragon: These are Charm dice, right? So in a vacuum (ignoring the other melee charms that interact with it, such as PCDM), the main practical benefit is that this saves you motes on the attack? Also, the 'After a successful withering attack' bit means that this is one of those charms that you don't have to declare before rolls happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Charm dice. One initiative for one mote isn't a great exchange, but battles are won and lost on mote efficiency. It is used after the hit, so you are effectively waiving the initiative point you gain for a successful withering attack.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thinking about it, I added in a little edge benefit to using Way of the Dragon in attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crimson Lotus Rebuke: Since using this charm takes up your next combat action if you've already gone this round, what happens if, say, three different people try to stick you with a Decisive attack in the same round and you try to clash them all? Do you lose only your next action, or the next three?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make it one use per turn to avoid this issue. The reflexive clash that consumes an action is a feature of the Terrestrial keyworded clash MA Charms, so I thought it best to leave it be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garda Wing Technique: The attacks are rolled seperately, right? Not one roll applied to both targets? Do both attacks have to be augmented by charms separately?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. I did consider doing it as a single attack but... hm. Actually, why not, changed it. Single attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury: The double 9's benefit to decisive attacks is on the to-hit portion, not damage? The wording is a little unclear so I'm not entirely sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World-Bearing Cataclysm Edge: The Final Flash counterattack is still paid for as normal, not free, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. You do get an influx of motes from clashing the ranged attack and your anima is flared up, so it is at least discounted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twin-Rivers Elision Flash: Not actually a mechanics question, but back in your dodge charmset, most of the various afterimage anima trickery was air-aspected, so I'm curious why you made something which seems very similar into a water charm here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point, but I consider illusions a valid component of both Air and Water Charms. They both have traditionally &quot;sneaky&quot; Abilities, Stealth and Larceny respectively. My Larceny set had one or two Water illusion Charms, so it's not entirely without precedent.<br /> <br /> Besides, I really wanted a lite version of the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oiFDnDmLyII\" target=\"_blank\">Tsubame Gaeshi</a> and this seemed like the best place to put it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948249#post948249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really enjoying the hell out of your work overall, and I expect to put it to some use in my campaign in the coming weeks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. At my current rate I won't be done for months yet, but I'm hopeful I'll see it through.<br /> <br /> Unrelated, in response to the worries about All For One, I've edited it slightly; each prior successful attack adds +1 non-Charm die to the attack. Because your allies already landed hits, I don't think the cap-breaking accuracy is as much of an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:18:14-07:00","id":948502,"title":"","content":"I think Melee is too weak at onslaught penalty reduction (dodge as well, actually). Fuel for the Pyre and Water Shedding Sword can only be used on successful parries or attacks and each negates a single point of penalty. They are fine as entry-level charms; FotP provides a nice bonus to Way of the Dragon, and WSS negates any kind of penalty proactively, but there isn't any essence 2+ option with a bit more power and cost.<br /> <br /> Judging from MA (I'm deliberately ignoring the QCs) terrestrials by the book get fairly decent onslaught reduction options; Revolving Crescent Defense in White Reaper to the very powerful Harmony in Opposition Stance in Silver voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:45:14-07:00","id":948518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/945466-a-clutch-of-dragons-dragon-blooded-melee?p=948502#post948502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Melee is too weak at onslaught penalty reduction (dodge as well, actually). Fuel for the Pyre and Water Shedding Sword can only be used on successful parries or attacks and each negates a single point of penalty. They are fine as entry-level charms; FotP provides a nice bonus to Way of the Dragon, and WSS negates any kind of penalty proactively, but there isn't any essence 2+ option with a bit more power and cost.<br /> <br /> Judging from MA (I'm deliberately ignoring the QCs) terrestrials by the book get fairly decent onslaught reduction options; Revolving Crescent Defense in White Reaper to the very powerful Harmony in Opposition Stance in Silver voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I deliberately avoided easy penalty negation in the DB set, and Melee particularly is not designed to offer strong always-applicable defences like Solar Melee is. Still, I suppose I may have gone overboard in keeping defensive options light. Something like Harmony in Opposition Stance would be at home in Water Melee, and Revolving Crecent Defence in Earth. I'll look into adding more defensive Charms when I do my second pass at the end of the set.<br /> <br /> Check out Mirror of Cascading Rain and Raindrop-Cutting Counter, though. I have tested them with a Dragon-Blooded melee fighter in a real game combat and they served pretty well (before she was punched through the hull of her ship by a Heaven Thunder Hammer. She survived!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:51:48-07:00","id":949142,"title":"","content":"That is fair to leave melee light on easy penalty negation, I think its a valid design choice. However, dodge at least should have onslaught/penalty negation comparable to MA, or the only place DBs can get powerful (if less efficient) penalty negation is external to their charmset in MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}